# Documentation style (Markdown)

- The audience is always a human, prioritise understandability and brevity.
- Be precise, consise and genrelly simple in laguage, except when technical language is required for clear communication and/or understanding.
- Use one emphasis style per span; do not stack formatting that serves the same purpose.
  - Links: do not wrap link text in backticks. The link already highlights it. Write `[path/to/file](path/to/file)`, not `` [`path/to/file`](path/to/file) ``.
  - Bold and backticks: do not apply both to the same span. Use backticks alone for literals (paths, commands, env vars) when they are plain text; use bold only for plain emphasis.
- Do not use emojis, em-dashes or other non-ASCII characters.